    "## Cross-Encoder Reranking\n",
    "\n",
    "The initial retrieval step uses a bi-encoder, which retrieves documents efficiently based on embedding similarity. However, embedding similarity alone may not capture the exact semantic relationship between the question and the retrieved document.\n",
    "\n",
    "To improve retrieval quality, we use a Cross-Encoder. Unlike a bi-encoder, the Cross-Encoder processes the question and each retrieved document together, allowing the attention mechanism to directly model interactions between them. The retrieved documents are then reranked based on their semantic relevance scores."
   ]
